  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_031, 0.678 acc) uses scvi_n200 + resnet50 + multiprofile + avgpool + weighted. All other axes (profile, aggregation, fusion, RNA encoder) have been validated as beneficial. The one major untested dimension in this best configuration is the image encoder: ViT-L outperformed ResNet50 in image-only (0.227 vs 0.208), but we have no evidence for how a stronger image encoder interacts with the multimodal pipeline. Question: Does upgrading the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l (while keeping all other settings at their known-best values) further improve validation accuracy, or is the image contribution already saturated with ResNet50? Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean, single-variable extension of the current best, resolving high-impact uncertainty about whether the image modality can be leveraged more effectively. If it helps, it identifies a clear path to further gains; if it does not, it tells us to focus remaining budget on RNA-side improvements (e.g., scgpt) rather than image-side upgrades."
